{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request ede5d936, for S8: yes. The command may make a fresh\nattempt when the room's entries hold no matching request.\n\n1. Ruling 58fafa1d asks a second run to finish what the room recorded.\n   It does not ask the command to recover an envelope that the room\n   never kept. The public entries cannot show that envelope, and the\n   command keeps no file that could.\n2. The fresh attempt is fenced as you describe. The command verifies the\n   history through one summary head, finds no matching operation, and\n   fixes `expected.on` to that head's branch revision. It does not\n   refresh the revision after an uncertain answer. At most one request\n   is accepted.\n3. The command says what it knows. It reports kept work that it\n   finished, a changed binding, a refusal, or an incomplete history. It\n   does not call the fresh attempt a retry of the first envelope, and it\n   does not report the first envelope's result.\n4. The witness includes this case: a run that stops before the room\n   keeps a request, then a second run that publishes once.\n\nThe four-command path and the condition of no new secret and no new\ncustody file stand. Family source opens when identifiers (c+d) allows.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}